Id: no-random
Pattern: (\bnew[[:space:]]+Random\(|\bRandom\.Shared|\bGuid\.NewGuid\()
Subject: *.cs
Except: :!*SystemRandomSource.cs
Issue: 47

The same argument as the clock, for the other source of an answer a test cannot
predict. A shuffled shelf, a jittered backoff and a generated identifier are all
things a test has to be able to fix, and it can only fix them if they come from
somewhere it can supply.

The exception is the one implementation of IRandomSource, which #47 added, and
it is written as a file suffix for the reason on no-wall-clock. Nothing behind
it is cryptographic: a key or a token needs a generator chosen for that job and
this rule does not stand in for that choice.
